            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes, easily. A pressure washer strips cured polymeric sand from joints with little effort. Clean pavers with a hose and a broom instead. If you must pressure wash, use a wide fan tip at low pressure and plan to top up the joints afterwards.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How often do polymeric sand joints need topping up?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "A properly installed patio should hold its joints for years, with gradual erosion at edges, in drainage paths and where snow shovels pass. Inspect annually and top up the joints that have dropped. Needing to refill within a season indicates a curing, drainage or depth failure rather than normal wear.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
